UPDATE "search_executions" SET "results_admitted" = 1, "findings_note" = 'hitCount 21, read from the persisted payload (5bac867ff07f9895.json). THE PRIOR MIS-DESCRIBED ITS OWN QUERY: query-priors.md says Q1b "relaxes that one term and nothing else", but Q1b ALSO adds a disability-population clause and swaps the co-production OR-set (drops "disabled persons organisation", adds user-led / co-production). So Q1 vs Q1b does NOT isolate the audit phrase; it is two changes, and the jump from 2 to 21 cannot be attributed to either alone. Recorded rather than smoothed over. SCREEN: 21 titles; 13 are conference abstract books, proceedings or off-topic (COVID athletes, nutrition, schizophrenia, haematology) -- full-text search matching a word soup, screened out on title. Abstracts fetched for 4 (persisted 5a34679594815519.json); full text fetched for 1 (18ef7d575e63330c.xml). ONE NEW Co-1-ADJACENT AUDIT FOUND AND STAGED, NOT ADMITTED: Mactaggart et al. 2024, Int J Equity Health, doi 10.1186/s12939-024-02314-0 (PMC11562328), Luuka District, Uganda -- the Disability Awareness Checklist adapted in three rounds WITH eight Ugandan youth researchers with disabilities, who then co-facilitated the audits in pairs (one disabled youth researcher, one non-disabled peer). It MEASURES ramp slope ("For long ramps (over 2 m), 2-3 measurements were taken at various points along the length, and the steepest angle was recorded") and reports a FAILURE: "of three facilities with ramps, all reached the minimum required width ... but two were too steep and none had handrails, meaning all failed the overall accessibility criteria for a ramp." The numeric slope criterion lives in Supplementary File Appendix 2, NOT retrieved, so no gradient value is in hand -- staged for a batch that can read the appendix. The warrant is co-production of the INSTRUMENT and co-facilitation of the MEASUREMENT by disabled youth researchers; the authorship and analysis are academic (LSHTM/MRC), so a Co-1 tier must be decided from the full text against D-0178, not assumed from this note. Also screened in: Obrusnikova et al. 2026 (US park audit, curb-ramp completeness inconsistent -- also a Q2 hit, staged once); REF-01006 recurred (already admitted). Screened out on abstract: Soner 2026 (nursing students evaluating a campus, a pedagogy study, not disabled-led); Seekins 2022 (Google Street View remote access scoring, a method paper, no gradient); Perry 2021 (qualitative park experiences of older adults with disability -- lived experience, but no ramp-gradient claim). harm_finding=1 on the Mactaggart ramp failure. || ADMISSION LINKED 2026-09-28 by session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection: REF-01009 (candidate 126): Candidate 126 was staged PENDING-VERIFICATION from this search (batch 20) because the ramp-criterion threshold was in an unretrieved appendix; the admission edge was deferred until this batch retrieved that appendix and resolved the candidate. || RESULTS_ADMITTED RAISED 2026-09-28 by session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection: 0 -> 1, level with this search''s admission edges', "updated_at" = '2026-09-28 06:48', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection' WHERE "exec_id" = 93;
UPDATE "search_executions" SET "results_admitted" = 1, "findings_note" = 'DERIVE THE SCREEN YIELD, DO NOT QUOTE IT: python3 scripts/research/mining_screen.py --ref REF-01007 --compare (slope-strict and slope-strict-plus-motion both 0 on this run; slope-loose fires on the accessibility stem). THE ZERO IS THE KNOWN BLIND SPOT, NOT A THIN LIST: reading the 32 titles and then fetching four abstracts (persisted b7b928f29b468566.json) found the audit literature a title screen cannot see. STAGED: Martins et al. 2016 (Ciencia e Saude Coletiva, doi 10.1590/1413-812320152110.20052016), 90 Family Health Units in Joao Pessoa audited against ABNT NBR 9050 -- its abstract reports ''only 47.8% have a wheelchair ramp, of these 30.0% have maximum slope'', the first MEASURED-SLOPE compliance figure this pass has seen, wording ambiguous in translation; Mudrick et al. 2012 (Disability and Health Journal, doi 10.1016/j.dhjo.2012.02.002), 2,389 California primary care facilities on a 55-item on-site instrument -- exterior access ''generally met the access criteria'', whether ramp slope is an item is not in the abstract. NOT STAGED, read and set aside: Nischith, Bhargava and Akshaya 2018 (J Family Med Prim Care, 67 PHCs in Dakshina Kannada, AIC checklist) reports ramp PRESENCE (60 of 67) in its abstract, the same shape as REF-01007; Frost et al. 2015 (JRRD, 30 clinics, ADA site assessments) reports restrooms and exam rooms, not ramps. harm_finding=1: every audit read reports inadequacy. || CORRECTED 2026-09-25: CORRECTION TO THIS ROW''S prior_expectation, SAME BATCH. It says batch 19''s warning about audits and title screens was ''carried into priors.md P1''. It was not: P1a-P1f are about what candidates 123 and 124 contain, and none mentions the title-screen blind spot. The honest reading of the prior field is its first sentence -- no per-pass prior was written -- and nothing more. || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26 5.2d): mined_ref_id derived -- this row''s own query_text names exactly one REF id that exists in evidence_sources. || RC1/RC5 phase 2-data (DR-2026-09-26): result-payload link(s) derived from this search''s own query_text against the retrieval log, per section 2.1''s rule. (1 artefact(s)) || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: mined_ref_id set to ''REF-01007'' || CORRECTED 2026-09-27: result artefact(s) added: retrieval-log/session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa/265e92157feb3c35.json || ADMISSION LINKED 2026-09-28 by session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection: REF-01011 (candidate 129): Candidate 129 was staged PENDING-VERIFICATION from this search (batch 20) pending a Portuguese-language read to resolve an English-translation ambiguity; the admission edge was deferred until this batch retrieved and read the Portuguese original and resolved the candidate. || RESULTS_ADMITTED RAISED 2026-09-28 by session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection: 0 -> 1, level with this search''s admission edges', "updated_at" = '2026-09-28 06:55', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-28-research-batch-21-selection' WHERE "exec_id" = 95;

